[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and closed on 5 October: the parser is fixed and
the booking-v3 form is retired. Read one by one, its reports describe three problems. Two are now
closed. The third, a one-day shift, is still open: neither change touches it.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but not everything in it is fixed. Reports of a date one day off still belong to an open ticket.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: day and month swapped (7 April → 4 July). Came in by app, email, or a booking-v2 form.
  The shared parser read every date month first; our tenants write the day first. Fixed.
- **`hint`**: also a swap, but it came in through a **booking-v3** form. That form printed
  `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field and then read the value day first. People did what the hint said.
  The form is retired, so no fix is planned.
- **`shift`**: the date moved by **one day** (Tuesday 12 May → Monday 11 May). No swap does that.
  These are the desk's one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`). The reports point to time zones and DST.
  Still open.

The subject line tells you none of this. Read the body and look up the tenant: where they are and
which booking form they run. Intake's tag comes from the reporter's browser and is often wrong.

## Lessons

- A big ticket can be several bugs that look alike. Merging by subject ([0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) hid two of them.
- Closing the big ticket does not close what was merged into it. Check each problem against the fix.

